<title>CYPRUS: Hijacked Sudanese plane leaves Cyprus for Britain.</title>
<headline>Hijacked Sudanese plane leaves Cyprus for Britain.</headline>
<dateline>LARNACA, Cyprus 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Sudan Airways plane with 199 passengers and crew which was hijacked to Cyprus took off from Larnaca airport after refuelling and headed to Britain early on Tuesday, witnesses said.</p>
<p>Police said an unknown number of hijackers were on board the Airbus 310 which was hijacked on its way from Khartoum to Amman in Jordan. One had threatened to blow it up unless it was refuelled and they were taken to London where they intended to surrender and seek political asylum.</p>
</text>
